# Low Water, Act 2: evidence and shared flags. Director's file, 2026-10-17. Private.

@fact fisk.button
about: Fisk's specification: a keeper on duty to restrike Mother after any loss of supply, by hand, at the panel. He wrote it so that nobody could ever say no one was at the panel.
against: trust 25
by: the engineer

@fact telegram.draft
about: The 18:30 telegram's draft, in two hands: Keel's words, and the time added in another hand.
against: keel 20
by: reading

@fact ink.crake
about: The Alderman struck the restrike clause herself, in her yellow night ink, and said so.
against: trust 30
by: testimony

@fact wages.stopped
about: The Trust's ledger: the keeper's wages suspended pending a review that never sat, initialled O.C.
against: trust 20
by: reading

@fact masters.green
about: Three masters' logs: Mother seen green and weak from the bay for more than a year.
against: wenna 10
against: trust 10
by: the masters

@fact relics.counted
about: The reliquary counted against Mother's numbers: fifty-six of her prisms are in the Gasholder.
against: fennick 15
against: wenna 15
by: counting

@fact strippers.named
about: The people stripping the stranded barges, named.
by: Lamb's own eyes

@fact typist.heard
about: The Shelf's machine, with its sticking e, heard through a wall on the Ropewalk at four in the morning.
by: listening

@fact button.tested
about: The button works: cut the supply, press after the lockout, and the arc relights. Nobody was at the panel on Low Night.
against: trust 15
by: the test

